# D19 / I25 / R23: one child grid derives finite lines from one parent cell.
# Parent cell C = [1000,3000] x [600,2400], u/v divisions = 4/4.
# Child u coordinates = 1500,2000,2500; v coordinates = 1050,1500,1950.
# The u=2000 and v=1500 child lines are split by the hole; all child segments
# remain within C intersect F. Parent cell boundaries are not physical stops.
# I25: 2000/4 = 500 and 1800/4 = 450 are exact integer intervals.
# R23: parent definition precedes child; derived coordinates/segments are not stored.
surface 1 origin 0 0 2500 u +x v +y outline 0,0 4000,0 4000,3000 0,3000 hole 1800,1200 2200,1200 2200,1800 1800,1800
grid 1 on 1 main-along v u 1000 3000 v 600 2400
subgrid 2 parent 1 cell u line:0 line:1 v line:0 line:1 divisions u 4 v 4
